WEBVTT

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.020
Please, Doctor.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.710
Even if it's just a run, or just a single pitch,

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.970
I want to help my team!

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.280
Goodness...

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.200
You are such a pain.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.660
Then just the last three games of the season.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.300
In all honesty, I don't feel good about doing this as a doctor,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:32.590
but I'll help you get through these last three games.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.160
R-Really?!

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.370
However, if you feel any pain or numbness during practices or games,

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.540
you are to stop pitching immediately and come see me.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.610
Under those conditions, I'll help you.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.150
I mean, I also want to see the Hornets win.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.570
Thanks, Doctor!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.490
Good morning, Japan.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.570
We're live from Braves Stadium in Indianapolis, America.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.910
Shigeno Goro came to America on his own as an 18 year old,

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:15.580
and he's already grasped an amazing chance with the Hornets in his first year in the majors.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:22.220
The Hornets challenge the Coyotes for their first division win in twenty-five years.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:29.020
I'm jealous that you're already fighting for the top in your first year, Goro.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.730
Looks like the majors are perfect for you.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.330
Play ball!

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:42.760
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:42.760
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:48.060
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:48.060
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.440
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.440
the only thing I truly have

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.730
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.730
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:04.070
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:04.070
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:09.330
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:09.330
the season of the coming summer began.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:14.710
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:14.710
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:20.800
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:20.800
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:26.350
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:26.350
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.430
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.430
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:35.730
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:35.730
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:42.030
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:42.030
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.660
namida kareru made

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.660
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.710
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.710
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:58.040
namida hareru made

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:58.040
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:03.050
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:03.050
though I may lose my way,

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.890
egakikake no ima

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.890
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.390
kizamu

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:14.140
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.680
akashi

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.140
kono te de

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.880
Never Give Up!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.880
Never Give Up!

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.040
So this is where he lives.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:43.990
It's nice. Too nice for a student at a third-rate university.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.140
Hey, Tashiro. It's been a while.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.160
'Sup.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.750
Sorry for inviting myself over.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.020
None of my other friends have access to the BS channels.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:59.920
Fujii

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:59.920
Fujii

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.150
Sure, no problem. Come on in.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.380
In the bottom of the fifth, Czech, the eighth batter, will get things started for the Hornets.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.770
How's the game going?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:07.260
It's in the bottom of the fifth and still no runs.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.670
So Shigeno hasn't come out yet.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.550
Yeah.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:14.230
Seeing how the World Cup ended for him...

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:19.090
Yeah, it'd be great if he could end this season on a high note.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.190
Welcome.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.800
Hello, guest.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.240
Is coffee okay for you?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.720
Wh-Why are you here, Nakamura?!

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.290
Oh, didn't I tell you?

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.850
We've been together since spring.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.210
We met during the World Cup, oddly enough.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.300
W-Wait, don't tell me...

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.920
You live together?!

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:42.830
Oh, please.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.300
Of course not.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:50.340
I'm ditching class to watch Shigeno's game too.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:55.150
Shigeno's still the most handsome hero I know.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:01.280
I just have to settle for this guy because Shigeno has no interest in me.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.430
Who are you settling for?!

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:06.400
So, Tashiro.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.460
Do you have a girlfriend?

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.570
Really, I'm happy for you two,

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.740
and don't mind me. Really, don't even ask.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.830
Out!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.640
Three up, three down for the Hornets' offense.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.430
Neither team has scored after five innings.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.910
Now hitting, number 5:

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.300
Silva!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:30.790
Play!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.260
Ball.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.030
Silva's hit twice today.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.940
He's been hitting well.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.240
If they're leading by the end of the game,

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.830
they'll bring out Shigeno.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:53.580
If that happens, we have no chance of winning with the crowd fueling the Hornets.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.540
We need to get the first run

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:57.830
no matter what!

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.170
It's out of here!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:10.430
Silva slams the ball straight into the batter's eye!

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.060
It's now 1-0 for the Coyotes!

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.870
Oh, man...

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.770
That was a nice hit.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.190
Darn...

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.110
Damn, Silva's good.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:31.030
I hope you guys don't lose this before I get my chance to play.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.740
Ball.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.700
Ball four.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.620
Damn!

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.710
Calm down, Rosario.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.630
Safe! Safe!

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.350
Umpire!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.280
Oh, Coach Stacy's coming out.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.520
He's switching pitchers!

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.740
Is he bringing out my darling?!

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:00.660
"Darling"?!

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.210
He's not coming out yet.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.610
I guess I'll start warming up.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:08.430
Catch for me, Sanders.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:09.150
Sure.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.280
Ball! Ball four!

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.920
Two outs and bases loaded.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.170
You're kidding.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.180
Silva's next...

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.260
Bastard!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.480
It's out of here!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.220
Unbelievable!

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.370
Two home runs in the sixth inning!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:55.720
Silva's hit two home runs in a row, bringing the game to 8-0 with a grand slam!

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:01.710
Rosario's replacement has taken a beating, giving up eight runs in this inning alone!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.630
I—

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.750
It's... over.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.760
Who could have seen this coming?!

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.260
You're kidding...

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.090
What are you doing?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:19.370
The game's over before Shigeno even gets to play.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.520
Well...

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.040
I'd better get to work.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:23.730
Bye.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.350
Oh, man.

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:34.110
They were doing well, but now it's just a one-sided game.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.240
Looks like Shigeno's not going to be playing.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:38.780
That can't be...

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.190
Hey, has Goro played—

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.150
Oh?

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.610
What? What happened?

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.240
No way!

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.650
When did this happen?

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:01.970
Out!

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.770
Well, we finally got the third out.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.690
What a game...

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:10.700
I thought we could finally take the league this year, but look at this!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.810
In the end, we're still the crap team we always were.

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:21.580
Twenty-five years of being weak didn't even give us a chance to dream.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.820
What are you saying?!

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:27.420
It's not over until it's over!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.710
I-It got through!

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:30.830
See?

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:34.260
If we can get more runners and a few runs here, we might have a chance!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.130
Ow!

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:39.090
Now hitting, number 1: Keene!

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.050
Okay! Follow his lead, Keene!

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:43.270
If you lose here, you'll never live it down!

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:48.810
Out!

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:02.370
Out!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.380
All right!

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:04.790
Nice, Irving!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.210
Damn, even luck's on their side!

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:10.630
Well...

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.800
I need to go to my own practice.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:17.460
I didn't expect such a one-sided game...

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.970
Goro must be pretty upset.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.830
There's nothing he can do about it.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:29.900
Safe!

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:36.490
He did not...

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:38.820
Don't throw! It's too late!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:38.070
Strike!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.260
What's he doing?

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:49.340
That's not like Keene.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:53.250
They're all losing their focus.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.470
Now it's over.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:56.780
I can't watch this anymore.

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:58.830
They did well, getting this far.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:00.220
Time to go home.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:08.200
Aren't we used to playing one-sided games?!

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.270
H-Hey!

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:15.850
Aren't you still a Hornets fan because you've been believing in our victory all these years?!

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:19.700
Yet... you're all going to give up when we haven't even lost?!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:24.960
If you go home and the Hornets turn this game around, you'll always regret it!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.040
You, stop acting like a girl and start cheering!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.580
Y-Yes, Ma'am!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.440
Give me a break.

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:38.950
You can't steal bases in a one-sided game.

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:40.300
Don't take us for fools!

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.110
Hit by pitch!

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:47.140
Bastard!

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.770
He did that on purpose.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:51.190
Time-out!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.180
Sanders!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.570
Call the dugout.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:17.360
Now hitting, number 6: Irving!

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.170
What?

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.500
What's wrong?

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:23.030
Boss, the bullpen's calling.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.890
Time-out!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.180
Switch?

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:40.100
Is that what Watts said?

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.530
Hey, there must be some mistake.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.880
No one's switched me out yet.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:47.360
Go back to the bullpen.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.450
Hey, what's wrong?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.280
There's no mistake.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.740
Get off, Clark.

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:54.620
If you don't care about the game,

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.290
don't pitch.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.250
What?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.430
You hit the batter for having a base stolen with an eight run difference?

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:03.720
If that pitch hadn't hit the batter, it would've been a wild pitch,

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.260
and the third base runner would've come home.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:07.320
Huh?!

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:08.510
So what?!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:13.300
Are you telling me to just do nothing when they've got a huge lead?

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.480
Another run's not going to make a difference!

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.810
Yes, it is!

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:26.700
Can you say what you just said to all the fans who came here to see us win?

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:34.910
The fans believe in our miracle until the end, no matter how bad we're losing.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.670
Even if there's just a one percent chance,

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:41.510
they place their hopes in us and stay until the end.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:44.510
Yet

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:48.680
we, the players, are giving up?

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.220
Aren't you ashamed?

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.530
Sorry, Clark, I have to switch you out.

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:03.280
I've come out here twice this inning.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.830
If you want to finish a losing game, be my guest.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:16.930
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 14:

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.640
Watts!

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.500
Knowing Watts,

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.670
he probably couldn't stand to watch Clark's irresponsible plays.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:24.760
Yeah.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.020
Play!

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.090
For the fans?

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.580
Like you're one to talk, when you're leaving the Hornets!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.550
Strike two!

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.160
Maybe there isn't a big difference between eight and nine runs,

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:57.120
but if we can get him out,

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.660
we can...

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.330
We can still keep fighting!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.630
A squeeze bunt!

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:08.490
Don't fall.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:09.980
Don't fall.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.310
Don't fall.

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:16.100
Out!

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.850
Watts, third base!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:19.730
Out!

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:21.770
All right!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.020
A double-play!

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:28.860
Watts!

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.990
What's wrong?

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.250
Are you okay, Watts?

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.370
Is it your hip?

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:42.840
I really did it this time.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.840
Looks like I may have blown my chance for next year.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.770
Get a stretcher!

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:50.130
Right now!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.100
That idiot...

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:16.590
He shouldn't have done that with his bad hip.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:18.620
Stopping the ninth run must've meant a lot to him...

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.520
Watts...

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:24.530
Out!

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.800
How's Watts doing?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.460
The doctor's checking him out.

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:35.890
In any event, the game is far from over.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:40.890
Just as Watts said, how can we show our faces to our fans if we play like this?

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:45.560
Or to Watts, who gave everything to stop that run?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.090
Strike!

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.030
That's enough, Murdoch.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:58.080
Can't you tell how much he regrets it?

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.910
He's been with the Hornets his whole career, much longer than anyone else.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:08.750
He probably forced himself to play because he wanted to help the Hornets until the end.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:10.830
Foul!

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.550
If it's going to be his last year on the Hornets,

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:18.430
he'd want to win the championship even more.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:26.100
This is for hitting one of our batters.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.100
Take some of this,

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:29.270
and piss your pants!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.250
Hit by pitch!

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.990
H-He didn't dodge?

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:45.290
Now hitting, number 8: James!

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.850
Let's go, James!

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.210
Follow his lead!

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:58.500
The fans believe in our miracle until the end, no matter how bad we're losing.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.050
Yet

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.850
we, the players, are giving up?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.270
Aren't you ashamed?

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:07.820
All right!

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:08.600
Nice!

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.790
Let's keep these coming!

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.850
All right!

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.530
Watts'...

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:22.660
Watts' brave, risky play energized the entire team.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.870
Damn it!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.530
Man...

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.340
About time they took back some runs.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.230
The game's starting to look better.

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:41.300
It could go either way if they get more runs this inning.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.310
Yes, okay.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:47.990
Shigeno, you might be playing if we can close the gap.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.390
Let's warm up.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.580
Sure thing.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.730
Ball!

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:56.990
Ball four.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.190
Umpire!

00:18:58.190 --> 00:18:59.900
I'm switching pitchers.

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:03.130
Czech, batting eighth, went down with a hit to third base,

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:06.370
but then Robinson got walked, loading the bases with one out.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:13.250
Oh, the Coyotes are bringing out their ace, as a reliever, when he pitched just three days ago!

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:16.990
Losing isn't an option for either of these teams.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:21.480
It looks like Shigeno's warming up in the Hornets' bullpen.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.490
Both teams are going all out!

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:25.510
Honda...

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:26.610
Darling!

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:27.850
He's almost up.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:28.730
Yeah.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.240
Honey, look!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.700
It's Goro! Look!

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.520
What?!

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:37.440
Coming back to the top of the order, Roy steps up to bat for the Hornets.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.350
Play!

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:43.750
Gotta hit.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:47.450
I can't let the game end like this!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.210
Go through!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:52.730
Out!

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.440
All right!

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.170
Please, one more push!

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.260
Nelson!

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:07.760
Ball.

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:09.560
Foul!

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:11.890
Strike!

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:14.770
Ball!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.230
Foul!

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.610
Foul!

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:21.900
Damn.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:23.870
Ball!

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:27.170
Nelson's showing persistence.

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:28.970
That's 3-2 for him.

00:20:28.970 --> 00:20:32.030
Now, the runners can just start running.

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:32.970
What?

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:37.060
Damn.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.090
Safe! Safe!

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.010
Damn...

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:50.220
I must've hurt it when I collided.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.770
Now hitting, number 1:

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.310
Jeff Keene!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:56.640
Play!

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:02.280
We didn't get three runs just by luck or coincidence...

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:06.100
Murdoch took that hit.

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.870
Robinson made that tackle to save a double play...

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:16.500
And Nelson's persistence triggered Silva's bad throw.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:22.090
Watts left us with the attitude to never give up, which gave us

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:24.360
this counter attack!

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.490
It's out of here!

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:44.990
Keene gets a three-run home run in the bottom of the seventh, and the game's 8-6!

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:46.660
Yeah!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:49.460
The Hornets have closed the gap to a mere two runs!

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:52.430
This game is still far from over!

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:53.740
Just two runs!

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:55.150
Nice, Keene!

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:04.230
Out!

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:07.680
Murdoch hits a fly ball for the third out.

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:11.290
However, the Hornets scored six runs this inning,

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:15.660
and it looks like the Hornets are bringing out a new pitcher.

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:28.550
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 56:

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:33.560
Goro Shigeno!

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:51.420
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:51.420
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:58.140
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:58.140
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.350 --> 00:22:59.810
yume wo

00:22:58.350 --> 00:23:02.980
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:02.980
oikaketeiru

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.770
ground no ue ni

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:08.980
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:08.980
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:12.950
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:12.950
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:20.370
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:20.370
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:27.670
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:27.670
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:32.420
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:35.440
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.420 --> 00:23:35.440
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:38.050
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:43.100
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.050 --> 00:23:39.810
kizukazu ni

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:43.100
suki ni natta

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:45.390
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:50.230
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:50.230
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:52.820
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:57.910
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:52.820 --> 00:23:54.700
otagai ni

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.910
hikareteita

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:00.120
kono kimochi wa

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:07.120
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:07.120
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:15.240
Preview

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:15.240
Preview

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:14.670
Our critical game with the Coyotes has reached its final phase!

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:17.140
This isn't the time to worry about my circulation problem.

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:18.960
Just watch.

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:21.430
We'll hold them down and win the league!

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.900
Next time, on Major: Final Chance.

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:27.040
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:30.960
Next Time

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:30.960
Next Time

